        "A vector search service stores the length of every embedding it holds, and its search call returns only the Euclidean distance $\\lVert \\mathbf{q} - \\mathbf{d} \\rVert$ between a query $\\mathbf{q}$ and each document $\\mathbf{d}$. You want cosine similarities, and you cannot read the vectors themselves.",
