          "p": "where $y$ is the true class. Raising $T$ flattens $\\mathbf{p}$, and lowering it sharpens $\\mathbf{p}$. Some models learn $T$ along with the logits. Take three classes with logits $\\mathbf{z} = (\\ln 4,\\ 0,\\ 0)$, temperature $T = 2$ and true class $y = 2$.",
