              "p": "Line B has the narrower margin (its edges are at $\\pm1$, against $\\pm2$ for A) and pays $0.375$ more for its longer $w$. In return it removes the hinge loss of the two points that were inside A's margin. A larger $C$ makes violations dearer, so it buys that trade. The misclassified point costs B more than A ($1.5$ against $1.25$): a longer $w$ magnifies every score, wrong ones included.",
