              "p": "Note where the parameters live: the first layer holds $85\\%$ of them, purely because the input is wide. This is the standard motivation for convolutional layers on image input: weight sharing replaces that dense $784 \\times 256$ block with a handful of small kernels. One variant of this question counts weights alone, so check the wording before answering: dropping the $394$ bias entries gives $234{,}752$.",
