              "p": "The network has $234{,}752$ weights and $256 + 128 + 10 = 394$ biases, so $P = 235{,}146$ parameters and $2P = 470{,}292$ forward passes, each of $234{,}752$ multiply-adds. One forward and one backward pass cost $234{,}752 + 268{,}800 = 503{,}552$, about 2.1 forward passes. Central differences cost about $470{,}292 / 2.1 \\approx 2 \\times 10^{5}$ times as much, and their answers are only approximate. That gap, a fixed small multiple of the forward pass against one forward pass per parameter, is the reason networks are trained by backpropagation, and why finite differences are used only to check a backward pass on a few entries.",
