              "p": "The AUC prefers model A, so it disagrees. Every pair counts the same $1/20$, wherever the two claims sit. All four of model A's wrong pairs involve its rank 1 claim, the first claim the investigator opens. Model B has six wrong pairs: the genuine claims at ranks 3 and 4 each sit above the frauds at ranks 5 and 8, and the genuine claims at ranks 6 and 7 each sit above the fraud at rank 8. None of them involves the top two claims, so none changes what the investigator sees. The investigator's own number is the count of frauds in the top two.",
