              "p": "Cross-validation prefers P by $0.0025$, while on the full 500 rows Q is better by 0.003. The two models cross at $m = (13 - 2) / (0.030 - 0.005) = 440$ rows. Cross-validation measures each model at 400, below the crossing, and the final model is trained at 500, above it, so it picks the model that is better for a size nobody will use.",
