              "p": "So the run you watched, at $\\eta = 0.16$, is already past the one-step rate $1/a = 0.1$, which is why it overshoots. It still converges, because $0.16$ is below $0.2$. Raising the rate by a quarter, to $0.2$, would stop it.",
