              "p": "After non-maximum suppression the order is D, A, F, E. Only A is a true positive, at rank 2, and $\\text{AP} = (1/2) / 4 = 0.125$, half as much. Non-maximum suppression keeps the most confident box, not the best placed one, and in image 2 it threw away C, the only box good enough at this threshold.",
