              "p": "The two agree, and they always will. Raising to the power $1/\\tau$ never changes the order of the probabilities, so top-$k$ keeps the same $k$ tokens whichever comes first. On those tokens both pipelines end with each $p_i^{1/\\tau}$ divided by their sum, because a renormalization in the middle multiplies all of them by one constant, which the final renormalization removes. Top-$p$ is different because its cutoff depends on the values of the probabilities and not only on their order, and the temperature changes those values. The order can matter for top-$p$ and never matters for top-$k$.",
