      "id": "pg-credit-across-one-episode",
      "moduleId": "policy-gradients",
      "title": "Credit Across One Episode",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "minutes": 12,
      "overview": [
        "An agent moves between two positions, A and B, and in each it chooses left or right. Its policy is a softmax over two logits per position, $\\theta[s, \\text{left}]$ and $\\theta[s, \\text{right}]$, so that",
      ],
      "setup": [
        {
          "tex": "\\frac{\\partial \\log \\pi_\\theta(a \\mid s)}{\\partial \\theta[s, b]} = \\mathbb{1}[a = b] - \\pi_\\theta(b \\mid s) ,",
        },
        {
          "p": "while the logits of the other position do not affect $\\log \\pi_\\theta(a \\mid s)$ at all. At the current $\\theta$, $\\pi(\\text{right} \\mid A) = 0.6$ and $\\pi(\\text{left} \\mid B) = 0.5$. One episode, with no discounting ($\\gamma = 1$), runs as follows and then ends.",
        },
        {
          "tex": "\\begin{array}{cccc}\n\\text{Step $t$} & \\text{Position} & \\text{Action} & \\text{Reward $r_t$} \\\\ \\hline\n0 & \\text{A} & \\text{right} & +5 \\\\\n1 & \\text{B} & \\text{left} & 0 \\\\\n2 & \\text{A} & \\text{left} & -2\n\\end{array}",
        },
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "1.1",
          "kind": "computation",
          "requirement": "Reasoning is not required.",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "p": "Form the single-episode REINFORCE estimate with the reward-to-go $G_t$ as the weight of step $t$. What is its component for $\\theta[A, \\text{right}]$?",
            },
          ],
          "answer": [
            {
              "p": "The rewards-to-go are $G_0 = 5 + 0 - 2 = 3$, $G_1 = -2$ and $G_2 = -2$.",
            },
            {
              "p": "Position A is visited twice, at steps 0 and 2, and both visits involve $\\theta[A, \\text{right}]$. Step 1 at B involves only B's logits.",
            },
            {
              "list": [
                "Step 0 took right: $\\partial \\log \\pi / \\partial \\theta[A, \\text{right}] = 1 - 0.6 = 0.4$, weighted by $G_0 = 3$, gives $1.2$.",
                "Step 2 took left: $\\partial \\log \\pi / \\partial \\theta[A, \\text{right}] = 0 - 0.6 = -0.6$, weighted by $G_2 = -2$, gives $1.2$.",
              ],
            },
            {
              "p": "The component is $1.2 + 1.2 = 2.4$. Counting only the first visit to A gives 1.2. With two actions the two derivatives at a position are opposite, so the $\\theta[A, \\text{left}]$ component is $-2.4$.",
            },
            {
              "result": "2.4",
            },
          ],
        },
        {
          "id": "1.2",
          "kind": "computation",
          "requirement": "Reasoning is not required.",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "p": "Now weight every step by the full return $R(\\tau)$ instead. What is the component for $\\theta[A, \\text{right}]$?",
            },
          ],
          "answer": [
            {
              "p": "$R(\\tau) = 5 + 0 - 2 = 3$ for every step, so",
            },
            {
              "tex": "3 \\times 0.4 + 3 \\times (-0.6) = 1.2 - 1.8 = -0.6 .",
            },
            {
              "p": "The sign has flipped: this estimate makes left more likely at A, while the reward-to-go estimate makes right more likely.",
            },
            {
              "result": "$-0.6$",
            },
          ],
        },
        {
          "id": "1.3",
          "kind": "derivation",
          "requirement": "A complete derivation is required.",
          "prompt": [
            {
              "p": "Say which actions each estimate pushes up for this episode, why the reward-to-go reading of the episode is the sensible one, and why the two estimates still have the same expected value.",
            },
          ],
          "answer": [
            {
              "p": "With the full return every step has weight $+3$, and each term pushes up the action it scored: right at A in step 0, left at B, and left at A in step 2. The left at step 2 is credited with the $+5$ earned at step 0, before it was taken. The terms at A are the ones that decide the net effect, and there the two visits pull in opposite directions: $3 \\times 0.4$ for right against $3 \\times 0.6$ for left, so the larger score of the left step wins and left ends up pushed up while right is pushed down.",
            },
            {
              "p": "With reward-to-go, the right at step 0 keeps its weight of $+3$, because it came before everything that followed, while the left at B and the left at A in step 2 get $-2$, the only reward that came after them. Both visits to A now push right up, and the episode reads the way it should: the move that earned $+5$ is reinforced and the move that cost $-2$ is suppressed.",
            },
            {
              "p": "The two estimates differ by the terms in which a step is weighted by rewards collected before it, here $5$ for step 1 and $5 + 0$ for step 2. By the time $a_t$ is drawn those rewards are fixed, and the score $\\nabla_\\theta \\log \\pi_\\theta(a_t \\mid s_t)$ has mean zero under $\\pi_\\theta(\\cdot \\mid s_t)$, so each such term has expected value zero. Both estimates average to the same gradient. This one episode shows how much noise the past rewards add along the way.",
            },
          ],
        },
      ],
